generalizedSplines -- the module of generalized splines associated to a simple graph with an edge labelling
***********************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = generalizedSplines(E,I)
  * Inputs:
      * E, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of edges of a graph (an edge
        is represented as a list with two elements)
      * I, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of ideals in a ring
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * RingType (missing documentation) => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value "Ambient",
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, module of generalized splines
        on the graph with edges E and edge labels I

Description
===========

This method returns the module of generalized splines on a graph with edgeset E
on v vertices, whose edges are labelled by ideals of some ring R.  By
definition this is the submodule of $R^v$ consisting of tuples of polynomials
such that the difference of polynomials corresponding to adjacent vertices are
congruent module the ideal labelling the edge between them.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[x_0,x_1,x_2]; --the underlying ring                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : E = {{0,1},{1,2},{0,2}} --edges of the graph (in this case a triangle)  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {{0, 1}, {1, 2}, {0, 2}}                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = {x_0-x_1,x_1-x_2,x_2-x_0} --ideals of S (elements of S are          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {x  - x , x  - x , - x  + x }                                           |
|       0    1   1    2     0    2                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|interpreted as principal ideals)                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : generalizedSplines(E,I) --in this case this is the module of derivations|
|                                                                             |
|o4 = image | 1 x_0-x_2 0                          |                          |
|           | 1 x_1-x_2 x_0x_1-x_1^2-x_0x_2+x_1x_2 |                          |
|           | 1 0       0                          |                          |
|                                                                             |
|                             3                                               |
|o4 : S-module, submodule of S                                                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|on the $A_2$ arrangement                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If edge labels are integers, generalizedSplines is computed as a ZZ module by
default.

+---------------------------------+
|i5 : E={{0,1},{1,2},{2,3},{0,3}};|
+---------------------------------+
|i6 : I={3,4,5,6};                |
+---------------------------------+
|i7 : generalizedSplines(E,I)     |
|                                 |
|o7 = image | -6  0   0   1 |     |
|           | -24 -12 -15 1 |     |
|           | 0   0   5   1 |     |
|           | 0   0   0   1 |     |
|                                 |
|                               4 |
|o7 : ZZ-module, submodule of ZZ  |
+---------------------------------+

The above splines may also be computed over ZZ modulo some integer.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : E={{0,1},{1,2},{2,3},{0,3}};                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : I={3,4,5,6};                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : generalizedSplines(E,I,RingType=>9) --computes spline module with      |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = image | 3 0 0 1 |                                                      |
|            | 0 3 0 1 |                                                      |
|            | 0 0 1 0 |                                                      |
|            | 0 0 0 1 |                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|      ZZ[]                       ZZ[] 4                                      |
|o10 : -----module, submodule of (----)                                       |
|        9                          9                                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|underlying ring ZZ/9                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Arbitrary ideals may also be entered as edge labels.

+--------------------------------------+
|i11 : S=QQ[x,y,z]                     |
|                                      |
|o11 = S                               |
|                                      |
|o11 : PolynomialRing                  |
+--------------------------------------+
|i12 : E={{1,2},{2,3},{3,4}}           |
|                                      |
|o12 = {{1, 2}, {2, 3}, {3, 4}}        |
|                                      |
|o12 : List                            |
+--------------------------------------+
|i13 : I={ideal(x,y),ideal(y),ideal(z)}|
|                                      |
|o13 = {ideal (x, y), ideal y, ideal z}|
|                                      |
|o13 : List                            |
+--------------------------------------+
|i14 : generalizedSplines(E,I)         |
|                                      |
|o14 = image | 1 y x 0 z |             |
|            | 1 0 0 y z |             |
|            | 1 0 0 0 z |             |
|            | 1 0 0 0 0 |             |
|                                      |
|                              4       |
|o14 : S-module, submodule of S        |
+--------------------------------------+

This method can be used to compute splines over non-linear partitions.  The
example below can be found in Exercise 13 of Section 8.3 in the book Using
Algebraic Geometry by Cox,Little, and O'Shea.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : E={{0,1},{1,2},{0,2}};                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : S=QQ[x,y];                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : I={y-x^2,x+y^2,y-x^3};--these three curves meet at the origin          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i18 : generalizedSplines(E,I)--this is the module of C^0 splines on the      |
|                                                                             |
|o18 = image | 1 -x4y-x3y2-x4-x3+xy2+y3+xy+y -x4y+x3y2+x4-x3+xy2-y3-xy+y      |
|            | 1 -xy3-x2y+xy2+x2             xy3+x2y+xy2-2y3+x2-2xy           |
|            | 1 0                           0                                |
|                                                                             |
|                              3                                              |
|o18 : S-module, submodule of S                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|partition                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|-x5-x4y+x3y-x3+x2y+xy2-y2+y -x5+x4y+x3y+x3+x2y-xy2-y2-y |                    |
|-x2y2-x3+xy2+x2             x2y2+x3-xy2-x2              |                    |
|0                           0                           |                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

