postulationNumber -- computes the largest degree at which the Hilbert function of the graded module M is not equal to the hilbertPolynomial
*******************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        v = postulationNumber(M)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, graded module
  * Outputs:
      * v, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, largest degree at which the
        Hilbert function of the graded module M is not equal to the
        hilbertPolynomial

Description
===========

This function computes the postulation number of M which is defined as the
largest degree at which the Hilbert function of the graded module M is not
equal to the hilbertPolynomial

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : V = {{0,0},{1,0},{1,1},{0,1}};               |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {{0,1,2},{0,2,3}};                       |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : E = {{0,1},{0,2},{0,3},{1,2},{2,3}};         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : M = splineModule(V,F,E,2)                    |
|                                                  |
|o4 = image | 1 t_0^3-3t_0^2t_1+3t_0t_1^2-t_1^3 |  |
|           | 1 0                               |  |
|                                                  |
|                                                 2|
|o4 : QQ[t ..t ]-module, submodule of (QQ[t ..t ]) |
|         0   2                            0   2   |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : postulationNumber(M)                         |
|                                                  |
|o5 = 0                                            |
+--------------------------------------------------+

