splineModule -- compute the module of all splines on partition of a space
*************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = splineModule(V,F,E,r)
        M = splineModule(V,F,r)
  * Inputs:
      * V, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of coordinates of vertices
        of $\Delta$
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of facets of $\Delta$; each
        facet is recorded as a list of indices of vertices taken from V
      * E, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of codimension one faces of
        $\Delta$ (interior or not); each codimension one face is recorded as a
        list of indices of vertices taken from V
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, desired degree of smoothness
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * BaseRing (missing documentation) => a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,,
        default value null,
      * Homogenize (missing documentation) => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true,
      * CoefficientRing (missing documentation) => a *note ring:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, default value QQ,
      * VariableName (missing documentation) => a *note symbol:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value t,
      * InputType (missing documentation) => a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value "ByFacets",
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, module of splines on $\Delta$

Description
===========

This method returns the spline module.  It is presented as the image of a
matrix whose columns generate splines as a module over the polynomial ring.
Each column represents a spline whose entries are the polynomials restricted to
the facets of the complex $\Delta$.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : V = {{0,0},{1,0},{1,1},{0,1}}                |
|                                                  |
|o1 = {{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {1, 1}, {0, 1}}             |
|                                                  |
|o1 : List                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {{0,1,2},{0,2,3}}                        |
|                                                  |
|o2 = {{0, 1, 2}, {0, 2, 3}}                       |
|                                                  |
|o2 : List                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : E = {{0,1},{0,2},{0,3},{1,2},{2,3}}          |
|                                                  |
|o3 = {{0, 1}, {0, 2}, {0, 3}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}}     |
|                                                  |
|o3 : List                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : splineModule(V,F,E,1)                        |
|                                                  |
|o4 = image | 1 t_0^2-2t_0t_1+t_1^2 |              |
|           | 1 0                   |              |
|                                                  |
|                                                 2|
|o4 : QQ[t ..t ]-module, submodule of (QQ[t ..t ]) |
|         0   2                            0   2   |
+--------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note splineMatrix: splineMatrix, -- compute matrix whose kernel is the
    module of $C^r$ splines on $\Delta$

Ways to use splineModule:
=========================

  * "splineModule(List,List,List,ZZ)"
  * "splineModule(List,List,ZZ)"

