  * "stanleyReisner(List,List)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note stanleyReisner: stanleyReisner, is a *note method function
with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in AlgebraicSplines.m2:2244:0.

File: AlgebraicSplines.info, Node: stanleyReisnerPresentation, Prev: stanleyReisner, Up: Top

stanleyReisnerPresentation -- creates a ring map whose image is the sub-ring of $C^0(\Delta)$ generated by $C^r(\Delta)$.  If $\Delta$ is simplicial, $C^0(\Delta)$ is the Stanley Reisner ring of $\Delta$.
************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        phi = stanleyReisnerPresentation(V,F,r)
  * Inputs:
      * V, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of vertex coordinates of
        $\Delta$
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of facets of $\Delta$ (each
        facet is recorded as a list of indices of vertices taken from V)
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, integer, desired degree of
        smoothness
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * BaseRing (missing documentation) => a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,,
        default value null,
      * Homogenize (missing documentation) => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true,
      * CoefficientRing (missing documentation) => a *note ring:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, default value QQ,
      * VariableName (missing documentation) => a *note symbol:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value t,
      * GenVar (missing documentation) => a *note symbol:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value Y,
      * IdempotentVar (missing documentation) => a *note symbol:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value e,
      * Trim (missing documentation) => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,,
        default value false,
      * VariableGens (missing documentation) => a *note symbol:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value true,
      * InputType (missing documentation) => a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value "ByFacets",
  * Outputs:
      * phi, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, ring map whose image is
        $C^r(\Delta)$ as a sub-ring of $C^0(\Delta)$

Description
===========

This method creates a ring map whose image is the sub-ring of $C^r$ splines
expressed in terms of $C^0$ generators.  If $\Delta$ is simplicial,
$C^0(\Delta)$ is expressed as the Stanley Reisner ring.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : V={{0,0},{0,1},{-1,-1},{1,0}};                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F={{0,1,2},{0,2,3},{0,1,3}};                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : R=QQ[x,y];                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : phi=stanleyReisnerPresentation(V,F,1,Homogenize=>false,BaseRing=>R)     |
|                                                                             |
|          QQ[X ..X ]                                                         |
|              0   2                                       3     2       2    |
|o4 = map (----------, QQ[Y ..Y ], {- X  + X , X  - X , - X  + 3X X , X X  -  |
|            X X X         0   3       1    2   0    1     1     1 2   0 1    |
|             0 1 2                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|             QQ[X ..X ]                                                      |
|                 0   2                                                       |
|o4 : RingMap ---------- <-- QQ[Y ..Y ]                                       |
|               X X X            0   3                                        |
|                0 1 2                                                        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| 3     2                                                                     |
|X  + 2X X })                                                                 |
| 1     1 2                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : H=source phi;                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : scan(gens H, g->print phi(g))--see the expression of each generator in  |
|- X  + X                                                                     |
|   1    2                                                                    |
|X  - X                                                                       |
| 0    1                                                                      |
|   3     2                                                                   |
|- X  + 3X X                                                                  |
|   1     1 2                                                                 |
|   2    3     2                                                              |
|X X  - X  + 2X X                                                             |
| 0 1    1     1 2                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|the Stanley Reisner ring                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The kernel of the map is the same as the kernel of the map returned by *note
ringStructure: ringStructure,, but the generators are expressed differently.

